WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.810
Most of the cells living on this planet
are not plants, animals or fungi, but

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.330
rather microorganisms called bacteria
and archaea. Together, they make up the

3
00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:09.830
prokaryotes.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.370
Prokaryotes come in lots of shapes and
sizes-- spheres, rods, spirals,

5
00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:22.530
crescents, even stars, and are usually
really, really small. A typical

6
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:26.420
bacterium like this E. coli here is
about 15 times smaller than a typical

7
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.350
human cell. One defining feature of
prokaryotes is that they lack the

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.580
nuclei and membrane-bound organelles
found in so-called higher organisms,

9
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:35.190
called eukaryotes.

10
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.620
Although this might seem primitive
compared to organisms like plants and

11
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.850
animals, prokaryotes were the first
forms of life on earth and so have had

12
00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.240
billions more years to evolve and adapt
than we humans have. And the evidence

13
00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:53.960
is literally everywhere. Prokaryotes
are in the soil, in the air, deep in

14
00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.620
the sea, in our guts, on our skin. In
fact, there are more bacterial cells

15
00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.600
living in and on your body than there
are human cells. Some live in extremely

16
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.560
acidic environments and some in extreme
hot or extreme cold. There's 7.6

17
00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:16.550
billion people on earth and 5 million
trillion trillion bacteria, 5 with 30

18
00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:20.910
zeroes following it. And although they
don't have nuclei, they can build

19
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.930
sophisticated structures. Some have
complex machines on their exteriors,

20
00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:29.530
such as long whip like flagella used
for movement, or small protrusions

21
00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.000
called pili, that they can use to
exchange genetic information.

22
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.560
And prokaryotes actually make up the
overwhelming majority of diversity of

23
00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:42.110
life on earth as well. For example,
strains of bacteria in the human gut

24
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:47.380
are less genetically related to each
other than humans and lettuce. Not only

25
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.800
are they extremely sophisticated, they
also make life possible. The majority

26
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.560
of oxygen in our atmosphere was first
produced by prokaryotes. They're

27
00:01:55.560 --> 00:02:00.090
essential for plants to grow, for us to
digest food. Without prokaryotes, we

28
00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:01.210
wouldn't exist.

